I need a python script that converts *.streamdeckprofile files with actions from the PilotsDeck plugin (see https://github.com/Fragtality/PilotsDeck/tree/master) into profiles that are compatible with profiles that can be loaded using the plugin https://github.com/wortelus/xplane-streamdeck. Both plugins at the end allow me to configure the 32 keys of my Elgato Streamdeck XL device with actions for my X-Plane flight simulator. Each key can also be a folder of further 32 keys.

So, command line input params are a *.streamdeckprofile file which is a zipped folder structure of nested *.json files and images and the name of the output directory. The generated output is a folder structure that is based on nested *.yaml files.

The script should come with a separate configuration file that allows me to define a root directory for converted profile directories.

I analyzed the structure of the *.streamdeckprofile files and the target yaml-based profile directories and I can give these rules and requirements that shall be respected:

Original *.streamdeckprofile structure
- each set of 32 configured keys is represented by a folder under Profiles/(some UUID)/Profiles. This last mentioned "Profiles" folder contains multiple folders, each named with a UUID. Each of these UUID-named folders has a manifest.json that represents a 32-keys assignment.
- the name of the "root" directory, so the initial page of 32 keys loaded can be retrieved from the topmost manifest.json in the directory Profiles/(some UUID)/. It contains an attribute that lists "Pages". The first found page UUID is the reference to the "root" folder to start with under Profiles/(some UUID)/Profiles
- each button configuration is represented by an object within the object "Actions". the key of this button configuration is for example "0,3" which means 1st column and 4th row.
- the button configuration has an Attribute "Name" that represents the type of configuration. The script should converte the following configuration types: Cosmetic Key, Display Value, Simple Button, Dynamic Button, Create Folder
- manifests can be nested: one manifest.json can link to other manifest.jsons of a different UUID-named folder. This reflects the configuration of a button as a "folder" that can contain other 32 keys or even more subfolders.


Target profile folder structure:

- the folder structure is like this the root directory shall be the name that I provide running the script as a param (see above requirement). on the second directory level ther shall be 2 folders "icons" and "sd32". and a config.yaml (provided in your context). This is always static. In "sd32" there are multiple *.yaml files. the root yaml is called "actions.yaml". each yaml consists of an object actions and then multiple chilren. each represents one button config where "index" is the button position (0 is the first key top left, 31 is the last key bottom right, e.g 8 is the first key on the second row) followed by a couple of parameters that define the button functionality and design.

Conversion rules between source (the json-based config) and target (yaml-based config).
